      },
      "7.0": {
        "desc": "Factorization in number theory involves the decomposition of integers into products of prime factors. This topic encompasses the study of properties related to divisibility, greatest common divisors (gcd), least common multiples (lcm), and the distribution of prime numbers. Key concepts include the Fundamental Theorem of Arithmetic, properties of divisors, and the behavior of functions like the divisor function and the sum of divisors function (σ). Common tools and theorems used in this area include modular arithmetic, properties of prime factorization, and inequalities involving factorials and exponentials.",
