      "9.0": {
        "desc": "Determinants are a fundamental concept in linear algebra, representing a scalar value that can be computed from the elements of a square matrix. The scope includes properties of determinants, calculation methods (such as cofactor expansion, row reduction, and special matrix types), and applications in solving linear systems and understanding matrix invertibility. Key concepts include the effects of row operations on determinants, the relationship between determinants and eigenvalues, and the use of determinants in geometric interpretations. Common tools and theorems include the Leibniz formula, Cramer's rule, and properties of determinants of triangular and symmetric matrices.",
